  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The alkaline oxidative fusion is a redox reaction (undergoes both oxidation and reduction simultaneously) in which a compound undergoes fusion with itself only, in the presence of a base or an alkaline solution. </p><p>Electrolysis is a chemical process where an electric current is passed through an electrolyte, causing a non-spontaneous chemical reaction to occur, typically resulting in the decomposition of the electrolyte into its constituent elements or ions.</p><p>Alkaline oxidative fusion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> :<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Electrolytic oxidation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> in alkaline medium.<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
